{
  "index_test": "whole-animal-in-vivo",
  "index_test_evidence": "PDXs are a valuable preclinical research platform generated through transplantation of a patient's resected tumor into an immunodeficient or humanized mouse.",
  "decision": "include",
  "reason": "The study uses patient-derived xenografts (PDXs) in mice to predict human clinical outcomes, which fits the criteria for whole-animal-in-vivo index tests. The abstract explicitly states that PDX response to anticancer drugs in mice has been closely correlated to the original patient's susceptibility to these treatments in the clinic, indicating a quantitative measure of agreement."
}
